<html><head><title>Teambuilding</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-weight: bold" lang="EN-GB">Team building</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB">, or community formation, lies at the heart of transdisciplinary work. The following pages in the base camp will tell you more about the different dimensions of collaboration in a transdisciplinary environment.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"><span style="margin: 0px">Let’s start with the basics. Team building is essential in two areas of transdisciplinary projects:</span>&nbsp;</span></p><ul style="margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: verdana"><li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 24px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif"><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB">Within your project group&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><ul style="margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: verdana"><li style="margin: 0px 0px 0px 24px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif"><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB">From your project outward, toward as many relevant stakeholders as possible&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"><span style="margin: 0px">Starting with your own group: you’ve</span><span style="margin: 0px"> likely experienced</span><span style="margin: 0px"> that collaboration is an art in itself</span><span style="margin: 0px">. In this TRAIL, we return to this topic often. Working together in a transdisciplinary team is especially complex due to the diversity of team members — differences that must ultimately be</span><span style="margin: 0px"> merged into innovative knowledge.</span>&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"><span style="margin: 0px">Secondly, it’s</span><span style="margin: 0px"> important to begin building social relationships with the </span></span><span style="margin: 0px; font-style: italic; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB">field</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"><span style="margin: 0px"> surrounding the societal issue from the very start. This field helps you better understand the challenge and come up with</span><span style="margin: 0px"> solutions. Expanding your network also helps you find the right new people to join the project team.</span>&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"><span style="margin: 0px">In transdisciplinary work, it’s</span><span style="margin: 0px"> crucial to stay alert to missing participants and perspectives. When you take on a coordinating role, it’s</span><span style="margin: 0px"> up to you and your team to decide how to involve stakeholders in the project: as advisors, sparring partners, local guides, or researchers.</span>&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB">Under the </span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-weight: bold" lang="EN-GB">Theory</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"><span style="margin: 0px"> section, you’ll</span><span style="margin: 0px"> find insights from scientific research on team building and the motivations of participants to engage in multi-, inter-, or transdisciplinary collaborations.</span>&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB">The </span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-weight: bold" lang="EN-GB">Practice</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"> page will soon offer tools and approaches you can use to foster group formation.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-weight: bold" lang="EN-GB">Note:</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"> In-depth pages for theory and practice are not yet fully available on this topic. Some authors of the TRAIL tool are currently working on a review study of transdisciplinary collaborations. Knowledge from this study will be added here soon.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB">You can already check out an introduction to this new research and the researchers here:</span><a style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 0px" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.avans.nl/onderzoek/projecten/detail/scoping-review-transdisciplinaire-samenwerkingen"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="NL-NL"><span style="margin: 0px">Scoping review transdisciplinaire samenwerkingen | Avans Hogeschool</span></span></a><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="NL-NL">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin: 16px 0px"><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif; font-weight: bold" lang="EN-GB">Sign up for the TRAIL newsletter</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif" lang="EN-GB"> to stay informed about content updates.&nbsp;</span></p>                                                                      </body></html>